From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 19:57:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 080/190] segacd: a neighbor mispair re-consumes the stream
 instead of reseeking

Two hardware runs measured the wrong-grab distance directly: -1 and
+5. Not constant, so not pointer arithmetic -- phase noise. On silicon
the header registers and the block pointer do not update at the same
instant, and an unlucky interrupt inside the 13 ms window records one
sector's header against its neighbor's pointer. Emulators latch the
pair atomically and cannot see it.

When the caught wrong sector is a neighbor (within seven blocks), the
stream is exactly where it should be and every lap re-inserts the
wanted sector with a freshly paired pointer -- so the fetch now goes
back to consuming the stream, bounded at eight tries, instead of
burning an attempt on a pause-and-reseek that arrives back in the same
phase trap.

The early ring-hit path jumps past the per-attempt setup, so the wait
loop's state is now initialised at entry -- the goto made a latent
uninitialised-read reachable.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 7dd8b5c..423e22a 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -1726,9 +1726,16 @@ static BOOL cd_fetch(ULONG lba)
     UWORD pt;
     int attempt;
     UBYTE settle, seen;
-    UBYTE why1;
+    UBYTE why1, wrongs;
     BOOL got = FALSE;
 
+    /* The early ring-hit path jumps straight to the transfer, past the
+     * per-attempt setup -- so everything the wait loop reads must hold
+     * sane values from here. */
+    settle = seen = cdd_irqs;
+    why1 = 0;
+    wrongs = 0;
+
     /* Take the drive. The VBL rotates a status question at the CDD
      * every thirty-two frames, and a question is a command like any
      * other: queued while a read is in flight it replaces the read, or
@@ -1841,6 +1848,8 @@ static BOOL cd_fetch(ULONG lba)
         seen = settle;
         cd_badrun = 0;
         why1 = 0;
+        wrongs = 0;
+rewait:
         while (cd_budget > 0 && cd_time_left()) {
             cd_budget--;
             if (cd_ring_find(lba, &pt))
@@ -1983,6 +1992,23 @@ collect:
                 cd_wrongdelta = (WORD)got;
                 cd_wrongsec++;
                 cd_why = (UWORD)((cd_why << 4) | 5);
+
+                /* A wrong grab that delivered a NEIGHBOR is not a lost
+                 * drive, it is a mispaired pointer: on silicon the
+                 * header registers and the block pointer do not update
+                 * at the same instant, so an unlucky read inside the
+                 * 13 ms window records sector N's header with N-1's
+                 * pointer -- the last two hardware runs measured the
+                 * mispair directly, -1 and +5. The stream is still
+                 * exactly where it should be, and every lap re-inserts
+                 * the wanted sector with a freshly paired pointer. So
+                 * go back to consuming the stream instead of burning an
+                 * attempt on a pause-and-reseek that arrives back in
+                 * the same phase trap. Bounded, then the attempt loop
+                 * takes over as before. */
+                if (got >= -7L && got <= 7L && ++wrongs <= 8
+                        && cd_time_left())
+                    goto rewait;
             }
         } else {
             cd_streaming = 0;           /* the transfer is what failed */
